 "doc": "PATCH_LATS (7), PATCH_LONS (-180..135 step 45), PATCH_N, and the scalars named in params.names (PATCH_HALF_DEG, EARTH_RADIUS_KM, SURFACE_LAT_MAX, SURFACE_SPREAD_FACTOR, SURFACE_FLOOR[\"itcz_lat\"], and the implicit 0.01 floor of every other judged metric). SURFACE_JUDGED order is in params. The port reads them from the source; this case says what the Python build used. The integers are exact; the float scalars are literals of the source, so their tolerance is close(rtol 0, atol 0): bit-identical.",
